    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0167" n="159" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1418: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Representative of the President</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-04-21T16:00:00-05:00">April 21, 1939—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:27 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. I have received the following telegram from Braden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“For your advice and with request that you please inform Licenciado
                            Zúñiga Montúfar, Dr. Rodríguez states that he will depart in a few days
                            for Caracas on Embassy affairs and he will there decide date of
                            departure for San José in agreement with Venezuelan Chancellery.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Ocheltree informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
